Title OSMGADisplay
Version 1.1
Description OPENSTEP 4.2 (i386) DriverKit display driver for the Matrox G450 (PCI 102b:0525, revision 0x80 and above). Five resolutions from 640x480 to 1600x1200 and four pixel formats, with the Storm 2D engine. The greyscale format additionally takes a Gray Levels setting of 256, 16, 4 or 2, which changes only the palette -- every value is the same 8bpp scanout. Installs the bundle into /private/Drivers/i386 and does NOT activate it: run Configure.app, add OSMGADisplay to Active Drivers in System.config, and reboot. Recovery: type config=Default at the boot: prompt to come back with the original display driver. The shared PCI ID also matches the G400, which this driver declines at probe -- G400 is not supported. 3D acceleration is a separate package.
DefaultLocation /
DiskName OPENSTEP MGA G450 Display Intel
Application NO
Relocatable NO
NeedsAuthorization YES
DisableSparseInstall YES
DeleteWarning Removing this package removes only the driver bundle. If it is still listed in Active Drivers the machine will boot without a display driver, so remove it from System.config with Configure.app first.
